111323","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-mc.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-mc[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Temporarily Disable LLM Providers[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Let users temporarily disable one or more registered LLM providers [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]from the ACE Models panel, with durable machine-wide expiry state, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]routing semantics that remove disabled providers from alias pools [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and ordered fallbacks, preserved-but-suspended alias overrides, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]actionable failures for direct explicit requests, and a polished [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]provider-management/countdown experience that stays responsive and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]visible.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]temporary_provider_disabling.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-mc[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-mc/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Add the Rust-owned temporary provider-disable state contract[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]provider-disable-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]provider-disable-core: add a versioned, lock-bounded, atomic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]multi-provider disable store and PyO3 bindings in the linked sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repo, then add the strict Python facade and lock-free display peek in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase. Cover concurrent entries, replacement, exact expiry, until-cleared[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]state, partial corruption cleanup, and binding parity.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make every model-selection path honor disabled providers[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]routing-semantics[dim] · [dim][/dim]after provider-disable-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]routing-semantics: introduce one routing-availability seam and apply it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to alias pools, ordered fallbacks, temporary alias overrides, default [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]autodetection, provider dispatch, model pickers, and completion [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalogs. Preserve direct-selection diagnostics, selector cursor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]invariants, and automatic restoration on expiry.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Build the Provider Routing experience in the Models panel[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]models-panel-ux[dim] · [dim][/dim]after routing-semantics[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]models-panel-ux: add a provider-routing modal, duration and exact-time [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]flows, live countdown/status rendering, background refreshes, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]affected-alias presentation, a top-bar disabled-provider pill, keyboard [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]help, focused interaction tests, and PNG snapshots at normal and narrow [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]terminal sizes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Document, stress, and land the combined provider-disable [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]feature[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]integration-and-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after models-panel-ux[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]integration-and-docs: reconcile cross-phase behavior, update the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]LLM/ACE/Rust-backend docs, run the full sase-core and sase verification [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lanes including visual snapshots, and exercise expiry, fallback, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]direct-request, and multi-process state transitions in an end-to-end [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]smoke matrix before landing.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-mc","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-mc.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-11ed2a9cefe409b0f1ef994408866efe","started_at":"2026-08-15T15:13:42.206184+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"3d2fb51e84c1a145cc0678e2d571f1181ad069d77a2bbfc8ab5459f50e9df192","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/chat.md","size_bytes":31197},"commits":{"digest":"0f459111be022dabdf357e168173e9a70c3dffdfe50a946d8c5bd84ed0790b57","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"3bccc87f267fe30dd93699b5dc51ac164b9a3f2187bcf8f368027dcfbfc3f981","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":66},"meta":{"digest":"7354d8d23a9ba423f211cfd7d5e57ef8e4997251d75ac91a02e0c8f532f5b352","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/meta.json","size_bytes":636},"prompt":{"digest":"6ba04d1c779fa50c21548306c1c360d816756954eb8a99d3bfcade68ff3b96bf","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/prompt.md","size_bytes":27624},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"4ec58500dea4719b8e43c7772dcbefbacceb344505741431c6786427fc24c9e7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/prompt_steps.json","size_bytes":6468},"state":{"digest":"2f339ce19f122c3a960b0d0a4062266e79aa73b48ba8be907f4f1423842234b9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1/state.json","size_bytes":183}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-mc.5.2--1","local_name":"sase-mc.5.2--1","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-mc.5","agent_clan_generation"